catholic charities of southern nevada  provides food and nutrition services for  the community as well as a simple way to  give back this holiday season  rocky spoke with deacon tom to learn  more  we are happy to spread this word let's  talk about the catholic charities of  southern nevada obviously you guys have  been around for a long time but some  people  might not know everything you guys do we  are going to celebrate our 80th year  uh next year so it's hard to believe  that uh not too many things are 80 years  old in southern nevada  right but one of them thank god and uh  we do lots of great things  thanks to a very committed team and  wonderful staff and great uh supporters  lots of food resources of food for  people that are homeless or food  insecure on the street  or working but the working poor the food  pantry is  a big asset for people that are trying  to supplement their income  especially under these difficult  circumstances that we're facing  and seniors more than 2  400 seniors are getting food every day  through meals on wheels  and obviously like you said these times  are extra sensitive so can you just tell  us a little bit more  about the food and nutrition programs  you guys have available especially  during the holidays  sure uh we'll probably distribute 3 000  turkeys uh between now and the  thanksgiving holiday uh we'll also  provide the fixins to go along with that  that's through our food pantry and  because of the pandemic we're uh  offering people to come and to be able  to receive those boxes of food  over a table so we're using social  distancing and sanitation  to keep the clients safe as well as our  team many people are taken advantage of  and  in many cases for first-timers i've met  people that were  resort industry folks that are either  laid off or lost their job and so  they're coming for the first time  which is great that we're here but sad  that they're coming  but those assets and those resources for  many of us that kind of take  the ability to feed ourselves and our  families for granted is really important  now  deacon tom tell us more about the daily  community meals and the outdoor dining  pavilions  we provide a free meal every single day  at 10 in the morning seven days a week  for anyone who's food insecure  families and veterans and folks that are  homeless and  people that simply are just down on  their luck or running out of food  especially  towards the end of the month we've  historically served that meal inside of  our dining room  but because of the pandemic and the  inability to social distance in there  we're building an outdoor dining  pavilion which is uh a big tent so it's  our catholic charities under the big top  in order to have about 300 people that  will be able to be seated  uh socially distant and serve this  community meal in a safe environment  also out of the elements and so that  meal will be served every day at 10  uh also the dining pavilion will act as  a day shelter  during the afternoon and it'll be open  for thanksgiving  so just a couple weeks away so we're  excited about it people are donating to  us again online  which is a wonderful way for them to  still be a part of this experience  and you know when conditions allow us to  invite volunteers back we we certainly  want them to come back  some people are volunteering by making  masks and scarves  um virtual volunteering uh which is  wonderful  and we're just grateful for people to  remember that  despite the fact that all of us are  struggling during these times there are  a lot of people in our community  that are really just trying to survive  and we're here to help them  catholic charities of southern nevada is  located at 1501 las vegas boulevard  north  for more information you can call the  number on your screen or visit  catholiccharities.com  there's more las vegas now just ahead
 

